### pasarelapagos-backend — fire-forget a marketing-attribution

Cuando `PaymentsService` confirma un pago (transición a `COMPLETED`),
debe emitir un job fire-forget a la queue `marketing-attribution`.

**Archivo a modificar:**
`pasarelapagos-backend/src/modules/payments/payments.service.ts`

**Patrón a seguir** (idéntico al fire-forget de analytics en chatia-backend):

```typescript
// Al final de confirmPayment(), DESPUÉS de que el pago ya esté guardado:
this.attributionQueue
  .add(
    'attribute-conversion',
    {
      paymentId:      payment.id,
      ecosystemId:    ctx.ecosystemId,
      organizationId: ctx.organizationId,
      revenue:        payment.amount.toString(),
      currency:       payment.currency,
      occurredAt:     new Date().toISOString(),
    },
    {
      jobId:    `attribution:${payment.id}`,  // idempotente
      attempts: 3,
      backoff:  { type: 'exponential', delay: 5_000 },
    },
  )
  .catch(err =>
    this.logger.warn(`[marketing-attribution] fire-forget failed: ${err.message}`)
  );
// NO await — fire-forget
```

